Difference Between writeFile and appendFile Methods

The writeFile and appendFile methods are used in file system operations to write data into files, but they differ in the way they handle existing file content.

The writeFile method writes data to a file by overwriting the existing content. 
If the file already exists, its previous data is completely removed and replaced with the new data. 
If the file does not exist, a new file is created.

The appendFile method writes data by adding it to the end of the file.
It does not remove or modify the existing content. 
If the file does not exist, it also creates a new file.
